  "section_notes": "Final rules are a red-line-compatible compromise: S2 gives per-model results to buyers and regulators but not the public, S3 sets a 6-year retrofit, S4 starts suppression at 36 months, and S5 uses the 8/100k mandatory recall trigger. S1 and S2 read safe; S3, S4, and S5 are acceptable because of the 72-month retrofit, 36-month suppression deadline, and 'promptly' notice language, with both flagship models non-compliant in one section each (Hearth 10 under S2, Ember 8 under S5)."
